SDP81_Band7_CalibratedData.tgz contains the calibrated uv-data:

* SDP81_band7_11exec.ms.calavg
* SDP81_band7_11exec.ms.spw3

To produce these calibrated datasets you will need to execute the calibration
scripts in SDP81_Band7_CalibrationScripts.tgz and follow the imaging script
that is located at the CASA guide page listed above.

SDP81_band7_11exec.ms.calavg is the spectrally averaged continuum calibrated dataset
and SDP81_band7_11exec.ms.spw3 is the higher spectral resolution calibrated dataset
that contains the CO J=10-9 line.


SDP81_Band7_ReferenceImages.tgz contains the CO J=10-9 line and continuum image products:

* SDP81_11exec.co109.R1uvtaper1000kl.image.fits
* SDP81_11exec.co109.R1uvtaper1000kl.image.mom0_2.5sigma.fits
* SDP81_band7_11exec.contR1.image.fits


SDP81_Band6+7_ReferenceImages.tgz contains the 1.14 mm combined Band6 and Band 7 continuum image products, which are uv-tapered to a resolution of 175 x 120 mas (see the imaging scripts for details):

* SDP81_B67.continuum.R1uvtaper1000klambda.image.tt0.fits
* SDP81_B67.continuum.R1uvtaper1000klambda.image.alpha.fits
* SDP81_B67.continuum.R1uvtaper1000klambda.image.alpha.error.fits

